{"title":"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Algebraic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Algebraic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At a party there are only single women and married men with their wives. The probability that a randomly selected woman is single is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca0718a644a517afe86b575e263feba13d34be03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. What fraction of the people in the room are married men?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c216bb4badf692aa1aeaeded8454956a1cb837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac13\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac38\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac25\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{12}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume arbitrarily (and WLOG) there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> women in the room, of which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bb3d7f40312b0590f5b89202e334e29736d5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot \\frac25 =  2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" /> are single and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36fda66ec7ffe5cfd5e861d0c129a627265a888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> are married. Each married woman came with her husband, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> married men in the room as well for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca37de60578e17f891939b7176e68bd4dc74e0e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+3=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> people. The fraction of the people that are married men is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b16fbd91edb4c3e2e6519b47c64e64e302fde16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"58\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Algebraic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Algebraic)\">Solution 2 (Algebraic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Algebraic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let single women be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, married wives to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, and men to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. As such, the number of men is equal to married woman since each husband has his own wife or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fe1ac9b3b23de9ebf32524665269fa8bc0b8e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />. We are asked to find the probability of men in the total group or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60cf6cfafc9aa5e99f1526731a02b2fbb6b92a02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{M}{S+W+M}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"102\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>We are also given that out of all the women, 2/5 are single or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/9/bb97ac0c10c19a4a0fe656ece5691e5fd80fac19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{S}{S+W}=\\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />. Rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967cc716650ec1f03851c33c22eaf3b030e8027d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{2}{5}(S+W)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fbe4afcac84b7ba6fd40e8777fa05e24cfd843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{2S}{5}+\\frac{2W}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />, isolating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbe2bf8044d2a753ad4a3e78dfcdeea23de9368f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3S}{5}=\\frac{2W}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"39\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/deffd17d724defa27959cac7daf6ddd9df54e84b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{2M}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"39\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fe1ac9b3b23de9ebf32524665269fa8bc0b8e53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W=M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />).\n</p><p>Now, substituting gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c3027012b5be21b782a48a3ac983689fdb17b790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{M}{\\frac{2M}{3}+M+M}=\\frac{M}{\\frac{2M}{3}+\\frac{6M}{3}}=\\frac{M}{\\frac{8M}{3}}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac38}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"349\" height=\"51\" />\n~RandomMathGuy500\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8\">2004 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017184002\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 171/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4041/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.030      1 -total\n 58.08%    6.987      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.15%    4.830      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11621:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017184002 and revision id 270828. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}